INSERT INTO posts(slug,title,description,category_slug,body_html,body_markdown,cover_path,author,updated_at,reading_minutes,toc_json,status,sort_order) VALUES ('electronic-software-distribution-(esd)-on-shopify-complete-guide','Electronic Software Distribution on Shopify: Files, Keys and Updates','Electronic software distribution is more than sending an installer. A workable setup connects the correct version, the buyer’s licence and clear installation instructions.','software-licences','<p class="site-lead">Electronic software distribution is more than sending an installer. A workable setup connects the correct version, the buyer’s licence and clear installation instructions.</p><h2 id="section-1">Keep delivery and activation separate</h2><p>BIG can deliver software files and licence keys. Your application or licensing service must decide whether a key activates the product, how many devices it permits and how revocation works. A delivered string is not an activation system.</p><h2 id="section-2">Package for the supported environment</h2><p>Name operating systems and versions explicitly. Keep Windows, macOS or other installers mapped to the right product variant. Include a version number, release notes and the support policy in the download package.</p><h2 id="section-3">Design an update policy before selling</h2><p>Tell buyers whether the price covers a major version, a period of updates or future releases. Keep previous installers where your policy requires them. Test whether a product-file update affects past buyers before using it for a rollout.</p><h2 id="section-4">Track exceptions</h2><p>Plan how to handle an empty key pool, a failed activation, a refund and a device replacement. Keep order and key exports secure. Only collect information required for the licensing and support workflow.</p><h2 id="action-plan">Your practical action plan</h2><ol><li><strong>Prepare the deliverable.</strong> Keep an original backup and publish a clear version. List the formats, compatibility and licence scope before the customer purchases.</li><li><strong>Connect and test in Shopify.</strong> Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.</li><li><strong>Choose capacity and monitor it.</strong> Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.</li></ol><h2 id="before-launch">Before you publish</h2><div class="site-highlight"><ul><li>The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.</li><li>A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.</li><li>The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.</li><li>Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.</li><li>Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.</li></ul></div><h2 id="where-big-fits">Where BIG fits</h2><p>BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.</p><p><a href="/features">Explore the features</a>, <a href="/#plans">check the plans</a> or <a href="/tools">prepare your next launch with the free tools</a>.</p>','Electronic software distribution is more than sending an installer. A workable setup connects the correct version, the buyer’s licence and clear installation instructions.
## Keep delivery and activation separate
BIG can deliver software files and licence keys. Your application or licensing service must decide whether a key activates the product, how many devices it permits and how revocation works. A delivered string is not an activation system.
## Package for the supported environment
Name operating systems and versions explicitly. Keep Windows, macOS or other installers mapped to the right product variant. Include a version number, release notes and the support policy in the download package.
## Design an update policy before selling
Tell buyers whether the price covers a major version, a period of updates or future releases. Keep previous installers where your policy requires them. Test whether a product-file update affects past buyers before using it for a rollout.
## Track exceptions
Plan how to handle an empty key pool, a failed activation, a refund and a device replacement. Keep order and key exports secure. Only collect information required for the licensing and support workflow.
## Your practical action plan
-
Prepare the deliverable.
Keep an original backup and publish a clear version. List the formats, compatibility and licence scope before the customer purchases.
-
Connect and test in Shopify.
Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.
-
Choose capacity and monitor it.
Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.
## Before you publish
-
The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.
-
A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.
-
The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.
-
Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.
-
Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.
## Where BIG fits
BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.
[Explore the features](https://www.bigdigitaldownload.com/features)
,
