INSERT INTO posts(slug,title,description,category_slug,body_html,body_markdown,cover_path,author,updated_at,reading_minutes,toc_json,status,sort_order) VALUES ('how-to-deliver-license-keys-automatically-on-shopify','Deliver Software Licence Keys Automatically on Shopify','A good licence-key workflow sends each buyer the correct key, keeps the inventory consistent and makes activation support manageable. Begin with your licensing model, then connect delivery.','software-licences','<p class="site-lead">A good licence-key workflow sends each buyer the correct key, keeps the inventory consistent and makes activation support manageable. Begin with your licensing model, then connect delivery.</p><h2 id="section-1">Decide what a key means</h2><p>Specify product, edition, activation count and duration in your own licensing system. BIG delivers the key; it does not make an arbitrary code valid inside your software. Avoid mixing trial and paid keys in one inventory.</p><h2 id="section-2">Prepare and map the inventory</h2><p>Clean duplicates and map keys to the correct Shopify product or variant. Keep a secure backup. Test which key is assigned to a controlled order and verify it activates the intended edition.</p><h2 id="section-3">Handle depleted stock and retries</h2><p>Know what the customer sees when no usable key remains. Do not let a marketing promise of instant access outrun your inventory process. Test duplicate or retried order events so support can distinguish delivery from activation issues.</p><h2 id="section-4">Plan exports and revocation</h2><p>Keep order-to-key records for support. A refund does not necessarily revoke a key in an external activation system automatically. Confirm and implement the process your licensing service needs; use BIG’s API and webhooks only on a plan that includes them.</p><h2 id="action-plan">Your practical action plan</h2><ol><li><strong>Prepare the deliverable.</strong> Keep an original backup and publish a clear version. List the formats, compatibility and licence scope before the customer purchases.</li><li><strong>Connect and test in Shopify.</strong> Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.</li><li><strong>Choose capacity and monitor it.</strong> Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.</li></ol><h2 id="before-launch">Before you publish</h2><div class="site-highlight"><ul><li>The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.</li><li>A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.</li><li>The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.</li><li>Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.</li><li>Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.</li></ul></div><h2 id="where-big-fits">Where BIG fits</h2><p>BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.</p><p><a href="/features">Explore the features</a>, <a href="/#plans">check the plans</a> or <a href="/tools">prepare your next launch with the free tools</a>.</p>','A good licence-key workflow sends each buyer the correct key, keeps the inventory consistent and makes activation support manageable. Begin with your licensing model, then connect delivery.
## Decide what a key means
Specify product, edition, activation count and duration in your own licensing system. BIG delivers the key; it does not make an arbitrary code valid inside your software. Avoid mixing trial and paid keys in one inventory.
## Prepare and map the inventory
Clean duplicates and map keys to the correct Shopify product or variant. Keep a secure backup. Test which key is assigned to a controlled order and verify it activates the intended edition.
## Handle depleted stock and retries
Know what the customer sees when no usable key remains. Do not let a marketing promise of instant access outrun your inventory process. Test duplicate or retried order events so support can distinguish delivery from activation issues.
## Plan exports and revocation
Keep order-to-key records for support. A refund does not necessarily revoke a key in an external activation system automatically. Confirm and implement the process your licensing service needs; use BIG’s API and webhooks only on a plan that includes them.
## Your practical action plan
-
Prepare the deliverable.
Keep an original backup and publish a clear version. List the formats, compatibility and licence scope before the customer purchases.
-
Connect and test in Shopify.
Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.
-
Choose capacity and monitor it.
Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.
## Before you publish
-
The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.
-
A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.
-
The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.
-
Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.
-
Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.
## Where BIG fits
BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.
[Explore the features](https://www.bigdigitaldownload.com/features)
,
[check the plans](https://www.bigdigitaldownload.com/#plans)
or
[prepare your next launch with the free tools](https://www.bigdigitaldownload.com/tools)
.','/assets/editorial/blog--how-to-deliver-license-keys-automatically-on-shopify.webp','The BIG team','2026-09-22','3','[["section-1", "Decide what a key means"], ["section-2", "Prepare and map the inventory"], ["section-3", "Handle depleted stock and retries"], ["section-4", "Plan exports and revocation"], ["action-plan", "Your practical action plan"], ["before-launch", "Before you publish"]]','published','15');
