ce scope before the customer purchases.</li><li><strong>Connect and test in Shopify.</strong> Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.</li><li><strong>Choose capacity and monitor it.</strong> Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.</li></ol><h2 id="before-launch">Before you publish</h2><div class="site-highlight"><ul><li>The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.</li><li>A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.</li><li>The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.</li><li>Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.</li><li>Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.</li></ul></div><h2 id="where-big-fits">Where BIG fits</h2><p>BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.</p><p><a href="/features">Explore the features</a>, <a href="/#plans">check the plans</a> or <a href="/tools">prepare your next launch with the free tools</a>.</p>','Shopify handles the storefront and checkout; a digital-delivery setup connects the purchase to the files or keys. Build the product and test the full customer journey before opening sales.
## Create a precise product listing
Describe the outcome, exact contents, format, compatibility and licence scope. Make clear that the item is digital and configure shipping appropriately for the product. Show a sample that reflects the actual download.
## Connect the product to the deliverable
Install BIG, upload the files or prepare access links and licence keys, then map them to the correct product and variant. Choose standard, custom or scheduled delivery according to when the customer should receive access.
## Make access visible
Check both the delivery email and the Shopify post-purchase experience. Use branded wording that states how to open the files and where to get help. A mobile test often reveals instructions that looked obvious on a desktop.
## Plan the first busy month
Estimate storage and monthly bandwidth, including repeat downloads. Choose a plan around the workload and required features. Monitor real usage after launch and before promoting a large video or multi-file bundle.
