INSERT INTO posts(slug,title,description,category_slug,body_html,body_markdown,cover_path,author,updated_at,reading_minutes,toc_json,status,sort_order) VALUES ('how-to-sell-music-and-audio-files-on-shopify-in-2026','Launch a Music or Audio Pack on Shopify: A Delivery Checklist','A music release or sample pack needs more than an audio file. Buyers need to understand the contents, permitted uses, file specifications and how to retrieve the download reliably.','music-courses','<p class="site-lead">A music release or sample pack needs more than an audio file. Buyers need to understand the contents, permitted uses, file specifications and how to retrieve the download reliably.</p><h2 id="section-1">Make the offer audible and precise</h2><p>Publish a preview you have rights to share and list the number of tracks or samples. State file format, sample rate and bit depth where relevant. If stems, MIDI or project files are included, identify them separately.</p><h2 id="section-2">Write the licence before the sales copy</h2><p>Listening rights, use in a video, commercial production and redistribution are different permissions. Explain the scope you are actually granting. Check rights for performances, compositions, samples and artwork before selling the pack.</p><h2 id="section-3">Prepare a scheduled release carefully</h2><p>A timed album drop can use scheduled digital delivery. Confirm timezone, file mapping and the information preorder buyers receive. Run a controlled test before promising that every component unlocks together.</p><h2 id="section-4">Budget for the complete download</h2><p>High-resolution audio and stems can make a pack large. Estimate bandwidth using the full purchase size and repeat downloads. Offer a readable contents file and a clear support route for interrupted downloads.</p><h2 id="action-plan">Your practical action plan</h2><ol><li><strong>Prepare the deliverable.</strong> Keep an original backup and publish a clear version. List the formats, compatibility and licence scope before the customer purchases.</li><li><strong>Connect and test in Shopify.</strong> Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.</li><li><strong>Choose capacity and monitor it.</strong> Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.</li></ol><h2 id="before-launch">Before you publish</h2><div class="site-highlight"><ul><li>The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.</li><li>A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.</li><li>The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.</li><li>Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.</li><li>Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.</li></ul></div><h2 id="where-big-fits">Where BIG fits</h2><p>BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.</p><p><a href="/features">Explore the features</a>, <a href="/#plans">check the plans</a> or <a href="/tools">prepare your next launch with the free tools</a>.</p>','A music release or sample pack needs more than an audio file. Buyers need to understand the contents, permitted uses, file specifications and how to retrieve the download reliably.
## Make the offer audible and precise
Publish a preview you have rights to share and list the number of tracks or samples. State file format, sample rate and bit depth where relevant. If stems, MIDI or project files are included, identify them separately.
## Write the licence before the sales copy
Listening rights, use in a video, commercial production and redistribution are different permissions. Explain the scope you are actually granting. Check rights for performances, compositions, samples and artwork before selling the pack.
## Prepare a scheduled release carefully
A timed album drop can use scheduled digital delivery. Confirm timezone, file mapping and the information preorder buyers receive. Run a controlled test before promising that every component unlocks together.
## Budget for the complete download
High-resolution audio and stems can make a pack large. Estimate bandwidth using the full purchase size and repeat downloads. Offer a readable contents file and a clear support route for interrupted downloads.
## Your practical action plan
-
Prepare the deliverable.
Keep an original backup and publish a clear version. List the formats, compatibility and licence scope before the customer purchases.
-
Connect and test in Shopify.
Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.
-
Choose capacity and monitor it.
Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.
## Before you publish
-
The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.
-
A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.
-
The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.
-
Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.
-
Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.
## Where BIG fits
BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.
[Explore the features](https://www.bigdigitaldownload.com/features)
,
[check the plans](https://www.bigdigitaldownload.com/#plans)
or
[prepare your next launch with the free tools](https://www.bigdigitaldownload.com/tools)
.','/assets/editorial/blog--how-to-sell-music-and-audio-files-on-shopify-in-2026.webp','The BIG team','2026-09-22','3','[["section-1", "Make the offer audible and precise"], ["section-2", "Write the licence before the sales copy"], ["section-3", "Prepare a scheduled release carefully"], ["section-4", "Budget for the complete download"], ["action-plan", "Your practical action plan"], ["before-launch", "Before you publish"]]','published','24');
