INSERT INTO posts(slug,title,description,category_slug,body_html,body_markdown,cover_path,author,updated_at,reading_minutes,toc_json,status,sort_order) VALUES ('how-to-sell-online-courses-on-shopify-without-a-course-platform-(2026)','Sell Course Files on Shopify Without a Full Course Platform','You can sell a downloadable course as a collection of videos, audio and resources. Decide whether that format meets your teaching goals before assuming a file-delivery app can replace a learning platform.','music-courses','<p class="site-lead">You can sell a downloadable course as a collection of videos, audio and resources. Decide whether that format meets your teaching goals before assuming a file-delivery app can replace a learning platform.</p><h2 id="section-1">Know which learning features you need</h2><p>Downloads can suit a workshop or self-paced resource pack. Progress tracking, quizzes, certificates, community access and student dashboards require separate verification. If these are essential, evaluate an LMS or a compatible course integration.</p><h2 id="section-2">Organise the lessons for self-guided use</h2><p>Use a numbered contents file, clear lesson names and a suggested sequence. Keep videos in manageable sizes and include supporting PDFs. Explain how to resume learning after closing the download page.</p><h2 id="section-3">Make accessibility part of the package</h2><p>Provide captions or transcripts where appropriate and readable exercise files. Test the download on mobile and a slower connection. A small preview lesson helps buyers assess format and teaching style before paying.</p><h2 id="section-4">Be precise about release timing</h2><p>A scheduled release can unlock a product at a specified time. That is not automatically the same as a per-student drip schedule. Verify the exact behaviour before promising a lesson every week after each individual purchase.</p><h2 id="action-plan">Your practical action plan</h2><ol><li><strong>Prepare the deliverable.</strong> Keep an original backup and publish a clear version. List the formats, compatibility and licence scope before the customer purchases.</li><li><strong>Connect and test in Shopify.</strong> Map the file, link or key to the right product and variant. Use the appropriate standard, custom or scheduled delivery mode. Check a controlled purchase on desktop and mobile.</li><li><strong>Choose capacity and monitor it.</strong> Use catalogue size and expected monthly transfer to choose a plan. Track actual usage and support questions after launch, especially before a promotion.</li></ol><h2 id="before-launch">Before you publish</h2><div class="site-highlight"><ul><li>The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.</li><li>A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.</li><li>The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.</li><li>Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.</li><li>Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.</li></ul></div><h2 id="where-big-fits">Where BIG fits</h2><p>BIG connects Shopify products with digital files, links and licence keys. It supports standard, custom and scheduled products. Paid plans include unlimited order counts, with plan-specific storage and bandwidth; API access and outgoing webhooks require Growth or Enterprise.</p><p><a href="/features">Explore the features</a>, <a href="/#plans">check the plans</a> or <a href="/tools">prepare your next launch with the free tools</a>.</p>','You can sell a downloadable course as a collection of videos, audio and resources. Decide whether that format meets your teaching goals before assuming a file-delivery app can replace a learning platform.
## Know which learning features you need
Downloads can suit a workshop or self-paced resource pack. Progress tracking, quizzes, certificates, community access and student dashboards require separate verification. If these are essential, evaluate an LMS or a compatible course integration.
## Organise the lessons for self-guided use
Use a numbered contents file, clear lesson names and a suggested sequence. Keep videos in manageable sizes and include supporting PDFs. Explain how to resume learning after closing the download page.
## Make accessibility part of the package
Provide captions or transcripts where appropriate and readable exercise files. Test the download on mobile and a slower connection. A small preview lesson helps buyers assess format and teaching style before paying.
## Be precise about release timing
A scheduled release can unlock a product at a specified time. That is not automatically the same as a per-student drip schedule. Verify the exact behaviour before promising a lesson every week after each individual purchase.
