rong> List every required file type, delivery mode, protection option and integration. Separate must-have capabilities from attractive extras.</li><li><strong>Test your own workload.</strong> Use the same product and customer journey across the shortlisted apps. Include your largest realistic file, a mobile download and an existing-order scenario if migrating.</li><li><strong>Price a normal and peak month.</strong> Use stored GB, transferred GB, order count and any provider-specific sales caps. Confirm the current billing screen and migration terms before committing.</li></ol><h2 id="before-launch">Before you publish</h2><div class="site-highlight"><ul><li>The product page matches the actual files, access and timing.</li><li>A sample or preview reflects the product customers receive.</li><li>The purchase, email and mobile access route have been tested.</li><li>Compatibility, licence terms and support contact are easy to find.</li><li>Capacity and costs have been checked against the current plan.</li></ul></div><h2 id="current-comparison">Keep the comparison current</h2><p>Our permanent <a href="/big-digital-downloads-vs-shopify-digital-downloads">BIG vs Shopify Digital Products comparison</a> shows documented features and monthly usage examples. For a broader shortlist, see the <a href="/best-shopify-digital-download-apps">Shopify digital download app guide</a>.</p><p>Published by BIG Digital Downloads. This is an editorial guide, not an independent benchmark. A feature absent from a listing is treated as not stated, not automatically unavailable.</p>','A fair review of Shopify’s own app starts with the current listing. Its capabilities have changed, so categorical claims copied from older articles can mislead a buyer.
## What the current listing documents
Shopify Digital Products describes digital files and links, delivery associated with products and variants, download limits and customer-account access. It is free. These are meaningful capabilities for a straightforward digital store.
## What needs more investigation
The listing does not document the same dedicated PDF-stamping, licence-inventory and custom/scheduled workflows that BIG describes. An undocumented capability is not proof that no configuration or integration can provide it; check your exact requirement.
## Avoid unsupported performance claims
A comparison should not invent complaint rates, outage histories or revenue losses. Test a representative file and inspect your own customer experience. If you have a failure, record what happened rather than assuming every merchant sees the same result.
## Choose the smallest workable setup
Start with the free app if it meets your needs. Consider BIG when specialised delivery or operational tools solve a real gap. Keep an evidence-based list of those gaps so the choice can be revisited as both products evolve.
